cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using these metadata."
title: pyjevsim
abstract: >-
  pyjevsim is a Python framework for Discrete Event System Specification
  (DEVS) modeling and simulation. It provides journaling, virtual- and
  real-time execution, and HLA federate integration through pluggable RTI
  backends. Version 2.2.0 adds a Portico backend, AT/SIM reference traces and
  application-state comparison commands for Pitch and Portico, and an
  experimental GORTI adapter that requires a source-installed SDK and a
  separately built service. GORTI observations are scoped functional checks,
  not complete HLA Object Management or formal IEEE 1516 conformance.
